{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1311 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a6d463d51412d4b4d28a11f5fd48807a252a11f4d809f185642b13a47bc01427" :edb/db-before-t 1310 :edb/db-after-t 1311 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534623 50 #inst "2026-10-08T02:45:14.195Z" 13194139534623 true] [17592186096677 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299460 13194139534623 true] [17592186096677 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299463 13194139534623 true] [17592186096678 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299470 13194139534623 true] [17592186096867 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534623 true] [17592186096867 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/e1b6599646532be14e417731c4a8b2f7c4dffcc475e2b99cda0279e7dbf08bc6.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-3{x}^{2}+5x$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=1$, shown above." 13194139534623 true] [17592186096867 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1040/Source/Images/q-11005.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y =-3x^{2} + 5x$, the $x$-axis and the line $x = 1$, shown above." 13194139534623 false] [17592186096867 1145 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-3{x}^{2}+5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+5\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+5\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-3(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+5(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186097198 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534623 true] [17592186097198 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/bd73ecb5633b2d3e43637ab5be7dacb6cd69d96957fbc199b0d59bbe6dbbcbec.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" 13194139534623 true] [17592186097198 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1040/Source/Images/q-49348.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y = \\cos x$ and the $x$-axis between $x = \\frac{π}{2}$ and $x = \\frac{3π}{2}$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" 13194139534623 false] [17592186097198 1145 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-1-(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299460 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299461 13194139534623 true] [17592186299460 1089 "q-345320" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299460 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534623 true] [17592186299460 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/927b979152097aef3939fa78738dbd2deb9d297cadf2d9894c19f31ca76aee1b.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+1$ and the $x$-axis between $x=0$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299460 1113 #uuid "901a6f11-447b-5c94-9ac6-eec54a15b2b9" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299460 1145 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+x){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\pi )-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+0) \\\\  & =(1+\\pi )-(-1) \\\\  & =\\pi +2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299461 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299462 13194139534623 true] [17592186299461 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534623 true] [17592186299461 1041 "field-1" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299461 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299462 13194139534623 true] [17592186299461 1110 #uuid "15d42f86-aed5-5605-85e1-b952c35280a2" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299462 1034 "\\pi+2" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299462 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534623 true] [17592186299462 1111 #uuid "21b97066-2f2c-5921-8b43-8c652541bd56" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299463 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299464 13194139534623 true] [17592186299463 1089 "q-54472" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299463 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534623 true] [17592186299463 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/eb35df379a8d7a20b9003218ee65e1cdcc3849af919805795dab380441d32795.png)\n\nThe area of the shaded region between the curve $y=3-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis is given by the integral expression below. What are the values of $a$ and $b?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{a}^{b}(3-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299463 1113 #uuid "bca0210a-1680-56db-b343-767175961d1b" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299463 1145 "To get $a$ and $b$, we need to find the $x$-intercepts of the curve $y=3-{x}^{2}.$ \n\nWe solve the equation for $y=0$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-\\sqrt{3}$ and $b=\\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299464 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299465 13194139534623 true] [17592186299464 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299466 13194139534623 true] [17592186299464 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299467 13194139534623 true] [17592186299464 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299468 13194139534623 true] [17592186299464 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299469 13194139534623 true] [17592186299464 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534623 true] [17592186299464 1041 "selection" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299464 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299469 13194139534623 true] [17592186299464 1110 #uuid "0510363d-9a97-5539-a060-21b35aa932d7" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299465 1034 "$a=0$, $b=2$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299465 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534623 true] [17592186299465 1111 #uuid "d3ef8ea1-c94f-50b7-95ba-dccfb90de2d6" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299466 1034 "$a=-1$, $b=1$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299466 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534623 true] [17592186299466 1111 #uuid "e32dbc9c-de4e-5a52-a897-a7867eeaa2a6" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299467 1034 "$a=0$, $b=\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299467 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534623 true] [17592186299467 1111 #uuid "c331e181-b4e2-57a3-99f0-ba0dccc61b83" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299468 1034 "$a=-3$, $b=3$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299468 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534623 true] [17592186299468 1111 #uuid "23709cc8-86bd-5d54-ad69-e2c7c903069b" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299469 1034 "$a=-\\sqrt{3}$, $b=\\sqrt{3}$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299469 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534623 true] [17592186299469 1111 #uuid "a09f0c3b-479f-56be-a220-0c7fc453e356" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299470 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299471 13194139534623 true] [17592186299470 1089 "q-73329" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299470 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534623 true] [17592186299470 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/d787ab7b213815ceb2cee11cf3f4a629c0f24b8328b33ae773be1e63f9f9a517.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=1$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299470 1113 #uuid "40d8392a-291a-59db-8a83-13f4cd515fda" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299470 1145 "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{-2}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299471 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299472 13194139534623 true] [17592186299471 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299473 13194139534623 true] [17592186299471 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299474 13194139534623 true] [17592186299471 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299475 13194139534623 true] [17592186299471 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299476 13194139534623 true] [17592186299471 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534623 true] [17592186299471 1041 "selection" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299471 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299473 13194139534623 true] [17592186299471 1110 #uuid "4d0aacdf-3497-57dc-8558-29fd6ca8953b" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299472 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299472 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534623 true] [17592186299472 1111 #uuid "117eeca9-3b82-5db9-98bb-283c60f71050" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299473 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299473 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534623 true] [17592186299473 1111 #uuid "b48673d8-0f48-5ae2-9c3c-3de91b9504dd" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299474 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299474 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534623 true] [17592186299474 1111 #uuid "514b4be5-6fe3-5aad-8d81-198ee63dcbce" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299475 1034 "\\pi " 13194139534623 true] [17592186299475 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534623 true] [17592186299475 1111 #uuid "053e5cc1-0229-5911-98f4-9827337634dd" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299476 1034 "\\frac{5\\pi }{8}" 13194139534623 true] [17592186299476 1103 #edb/ref 1759218604